#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:344
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Search in Files"
msgid "Search &amp; Replace"
msgstr "In Dateien söken"

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:347 plugins.docbook:1228 plugins.docbook:1412
#: plugins.docbook:1637
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Inföhren"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname;'s Search &amp; Replace plugin allows you to search for text or "
"<ulink url=\"help:/katepart/regular-expressions.html\">regular expressions</"
"ulink> in many different files at once. You can search all open files, all "
"the files in one directory and optionally its subdirectories, or all files "
"in the current project. You can even filter by filename, for instance "
"searching only files that end with a particular file extension."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:358 plugins.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search Query"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following options are always displayed at the top of the Search in Files "
"tool view:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guiicon
#: plugins.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Tab"
msgstr "Nieg Paneel"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can have as many searches as you want open at the same time. Simply "
"click the <guibutton>New Tab</guibutton> button at the top-left corner of "
"the Search tool view and a new results tab will open permitting you to "
"perform another search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guiicon
#: plugins.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toggle Results"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The down arrow in the top right-corner of the Search in Files tool view will "
"toggle the bottom half of the tool view between displaying additional "
"options for the Search in Folder mode and the results of your search."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:388
#, no-c-format
msgid "Find"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is where you type in what you want to find. You may enter standard "
"text, or a regular expression if enabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Replace</guilabel> (text box)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Replacement text that will be added to file(s) in place of the text in the "
"<guilabel>Find</guilabel> text box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: plugins.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Search</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you've finished configuring everything, just press the "
"<guibutton>Search</guibutton> button to perform your search. You may also "
"press &Enter; in the <guilabel>Find</guilabel> text box to do the same."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: plugins.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you've finished configuring everything, just press the "
"<guibutton>Replace</guibutton> button to replace the text entered in the "
"<guilabel>Find</guilabel> text box with that of the <guilabel>Replace</"
"guilabel> text box. You may also press &Enter; in the <guilabel>Replace</"
"guilabel> text box to do the same."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: plugins.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid "Next"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Go to the next match of your search query, switching files if necessary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: plugins.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace checked"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The same as <guibutton>Replace</guibutton>, but will only perform "
"replacements in files that are checked in the pane below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search in Folder Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These options are displayed below the aforementioned query options. If "
"search results are being displayed instead, press the <guiicon>Toggle "
"Results</guiicon> button to display them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid "Match case"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Restricts search results to only those that have the exact same combination "
"of upper and lower case letters as your search query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "Regular expressions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Permits you to use <ulink url=\"help:/katepart/regular-expressions.html"
"\">regular expressions</ulink> instead of simple text as your search query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expand results"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:468
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Display all the results found in each file, instead of just a list of files "
"that contain the search query."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Search</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This has three options. Select <guilabel>in Open files</guilabel> to search "
"all files currently open in &kappname;. Select <guilabel>in Folder</"
"guilabel> to search inside a folder and optionally its subfolders. Select "
"<guilabel>in Project</guilabel> to search all the files listed in the "
"currently open project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:485
#, no-c-format
msgid "Folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may enter the path of the folder you wish to search. For instance, you "
"might enter <userinput>~/development/kde/kate/</userinput> if you wished to "
"search the &kate; source code. This option is only available when using "
"<guilabel>in Folder</guilabel> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guiicon
#: plugins.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open file dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press this button to locate the folder in your desktop's folder browser. "
"This button only works when using <guilabel>in Folder</guilabel> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guiicon
#: plugins.docbook:503
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guiicon>Up</guiicon>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press this button to change <guilabel>Folder</guilabel> to the parent of the "
"currently selected folder. This button only works when using <guilabel>in "
"Folder</guilabel> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guiicon
#: plugins.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restore Current Folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button will set the <guilabel>Folder</guilabel> entry to the folder in "
"which the currently open document is located. This button only works when "
"using <guilabel>in Folder</guilabel> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filter"
msgstr "Filter"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This permits you to only search filenames that match a particular pattern. "
"For instance, to only search files written in C++, change it to <userinput>*."
"cpp</userinput>. To search only files beginning with <literal>kate</"
"literal>, change it to <userinput>kate*</userinput>. You can enter multiple "
"filters separated with a comma (<userinput>,</userinput>). This option is "
"not available when using <guilabel>in Open files</guilabel> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exclude"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The opposite of <guilabel>Filter</guilabel>, this prevents &kappname; from "
"searching files that match the specified patterns. As with <guilabel>Filter</"
"guilabel>, you can enter multiple patterns separated with a comma "
"(<userinput>,</userinput>). This option is not available when using "
"<guilabel>in Open files</guilabel> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid "Recursive"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, &kappname; will also search in all subfolders of "
"the selected folder. This option is only available when using <guilabel>in "
"Folder</guilabel> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "Include hidden"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, &kappname; will also search in files or folders "
"that are typically hidden by your &OS;. This option is only available when "
"using <guilabel>in Folder</guilabel> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: plugins.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid "Follow symbolic links"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
